DOLLY 7
PACKAGE llama
REQUIRES HOST runtime@0
REQUIRES HOST gpu@0

# dolly-llama as local-llm-build links it: llama.cpp with its WebGPU backend,
# serving the model it is given over stdin and stdout. A model package brings
# the GGUF.
FROM /v0.1.3/demos/local-llm/Dollyfile-local-llm-build 70b5b628a2cf9cc1c76832d2c833ea00e1ccb588ffdfca5732d8f6e253ec97fa

EXPORTS TOOL   dolly-llama
EXPORTS FOLDER llama-licenses /usr/share/licenses/dolly-llm
FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/dolly-llama.1
    dolly-llama: llama.cpp on WebGPU, serving a GGUF model to Pi (provider webgpu).
    
      dolly-llama MODEL.gguf    serves the model
      dolly-llama --check       prints the shader kind this adapter gets
    
    Each line of standard input is a request as llama-server takes it at
    /v1/chat/completions; standard output is the event stream it would answer
    with, and a field it does not implement is an error naming it. It uses the
    adapter gpu@0 grants: with shader-f16 llama.cpp's WGSL as upstream wrote it,
    without it the f16 shader code widened to f32. The chat template, tool
    calls, stop tokens and sampling defaults are the GGUF's own. Pi's /model,
    /thinking and /local choose and tune the model.
